Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: bq27xxx: report Full only while supplied

The bq27411-compatible gauge on the OnePlus 7 Pro keeps its full-charge
flag set after the charger is unplugged until the state of charge drops
below its clear threshold, so the battery kept reporting Full while
discharging and UPower treated the phone as on external power.

When the battery has a described supplier (power-supplies) and none of
them is online, fall through to the current-based status instead of Full.
Without a described supplier power_supply_am_i_supplied() returns
-ENODEV and the previous behaviour is kept.

---
diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/bq27xxx_battery.c b/drivers/power/supply/bq27xxx_battery.c
index ad2d9ecf3..6321d9b2a 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/bq27xxx_battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/bq27xxx_battery.c
@@ -1899,7 +1899,13 @@ static int bq27xxx_battery_current_and_status(
 		val_curr->intval = curr;
 
 	if (val_status) {
-		if (bq27xxx_battery_is_full(di, flags))
+		/*
+		 * The full-charge flag stays set until the state of charge drops
+		 * below the gauge's clear threshold, also while running from the
+		 * battery. Only report Full while a described supplier is online.
+		 */
+		if (bq27xxx_battery_is_full(di, flags) &&
+		    (!di->bat || power_supply_am_i_supplied(di->bat) != 0))
 			val_status->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_FULL;
 		else if (curr > 0)
 			val_status->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_CHARGING;
